          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "kip, a bundle or set of hides, skins or furs, used as a measure of quantity (OED s.v. kip n.1); e.g. a kip of lambfells reckoned at 150 lambskins. Frequently confused orthographically with kipe (a basket) — see kyppe."
    }
